-- title:
--   Ideals of A[x₀,…,xₙ] cut out ideal sheaves on Pⁿ_A
-- statement:
--   Let $n$ be a natural number, let $A$ be a commutative ring, and let $I$ be an arbitrary ideal of the polynomial ring $S = A[x_0,\dots,x_n]$ in $n+1$ variables indexed by `Fin (n + 1)`, graded by the submodules `MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin (n + 1)) A` of homogeneous polynomials of each degree. The assertion is that there exists an ideal sheaf datum $\mathcal{I}$ on the scheme $\operatorname{Proj}$ of this graded ring (that is, a Mathlib `Scheme.IdealSheafData`: an ideal of the ring of sections on each affine open, compatible under restriction) whose value on each of the $n+1$ standard charts is the expected ideal of dehomogenisations. Precisely, for every $i \in \{0,\dots,n\}$, consider the basic open $D_+(x_i)$, which is an affine open because $x_i$ is homogeneous of degree $1 > 0$; then the ideal assigned by $\mathcal{I}$ to this affine open equals the ideal of its ring of sections generated by the set of sections obtained, via `Proj.awayToSection`, from the degree-zero homogeneous localisations $F / x_i^{\,d}$, as $d$ ranges over the natural numbers and $F$ over the elements of $I$ that are homogeneous of degree $d$. No homogeneity hypothesis is placed on $I$ itself: only its homogeneous elements enter the generating set.
--
--   This is the construction of the closed subscheme of projective space $\mathbb{P}^n_A$ cut out by an ideal of the homogeneous coordinate ring, in the form of a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf specified chart by chart on the cover $\{D_+(x_i)\}$. It is used in the development of the Hilbert functor, where ideal sheaves on $\mathbb{P}^n_A$ with prescribed behaviour on the standard charts are produced and compared with kernels of closed immersions.
